{"id":12600,"date":"2026-08-01T16:12:27","date_gmt":"2026-08-01T23:12:27","guid":{"rendered":"https://staging.kosick.com/?p=12600"},"modified":"2026-08-01T16:25:01","modified_gmt":"2026-08-01T23:25:01","slug":"what-is-social-marketing","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https://staging.kosick.com/what-is-social-marketing/","title":{"rendered":"What Is Social Marketing? A Guide for Canadian Businesses"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Every business owner has heard by now they should be &#8220;doing social.&#8221; Post more, show up on Instagram, run a few ads, and the customers will follow. If only it worked so simply. Posting is easy. Building a social presence into a channel that actually grows revenue is a different discipline, and it has a name: social marketing.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So what is social marketing, really, and how is it different from just having a Facebook page? Here is a clear, no-jargon guide for owners and marketers who want the channel to pull its weight.</p>\n\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kb-btns12600_18b3bd-1f{gap:var(--global-kb-gap-xs, 0.5rem );justify-content:center;align-items:center;}.kt-btns12600_18b3bd-1f .kt-button{font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;}.kt-btns12600_18b3bd-1f .kt-btn-wrap-0{margin-right:5px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_18b3bd-1f .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button{color:#555555;border-color:#555555;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_18b3bd-1f .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button:hover, .wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_18b3bd-1f .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button:focus{color:#ffffff;border-color:#444444;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_18b3bd-1f .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button::before{display:none;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_18b3bd-1f .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button:hover, .wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_18b3bd-1f .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button:focus{background:#444444;}</style>\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn kb-buttons-wrap kb-btns12600_18b3bd-1f\"><style>ul.menu .wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn .kb-btn12600_2ed0c9-17.kb-button{width:initial;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn .kb-btn12600_2ed0c9-17.kb-button{color:var(--global-palette3, #1A202C);font-size:16px;font-family:Poppins;font-weight:400;text-transform:uppercase;border-top-left-radius:20px;border-top-right-radius:20px;border-bottom-right-radius:20px;border-bottom-left-radius:20px;border-top-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-top-style:solid;border-right-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-bottom-style:solid;border-left-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-left-style:solid;padding-right:var(--global-kb-spacing-md, 2rem);padding-left:var(--global-kb-spacing-md, 2rem);}@media all and (max-width: 1024px){.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn .kb-btn12600_2ed0c9-17.kb-button{border-top-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-top-style:solid;border-right-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-bottom-style:solid;border-left-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-left-style:solid;}}@media all and (max-width: 767px){.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn .kb-btn12600_2ed0c9-17.kb-button{border-top-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-top-style:solid;border-right-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-bottom-style:solid;border-left-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-left-style:solid;}}</style><a class=\"kb-button kt-button button kb-btn12600_2ed0c9-17 kt-btn-size-standard kt-btn-width-type-auto kb-btn-global-outline kt-btn-has-text-true kt-btn-has-svg-false wp-block-kadence-singlebtn\" href=\"https://staging.kosick.com/services/social-media-marketing/\"><span class=\"kt-btn-inner-text\">Social Media marketing</span></a></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Social Marketing Is Strategy, Not Just Posting</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Social marketing is the practice of using social platforms to reach a defined audience, move them through a buying journey, and drive a measurable business result. The result might be a lead, a sale, a booking, or a stronger brand people remember when they are ready to buy.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The keyword there is&nbsp;<em>result</em>. A random post about your team lunch might earn a few likes, but it does not connect to a goal. Social marketing starts from the goal and works backward. Who are we trying to reach? What do we want them to do? What message, on which platform, at what moment, will get them to do it? Every post, story, and ad ladders up to an objective you can actually track.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is the line between a business with a social account and a business with a social marketing program. One publishes. The other plans.</p>\n\n\n<style>.kb-image12600_24c41b-34 .kb-image-has-overlay:after{opacity:0.3;}</style>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-kadence-image kb-image12600_24c41b-34 size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1122\" height=\"1402\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Garden-Centre-Social-Media.jpg\" alt=\"Social Media Content Management\" class=\"kb-img wp-image-12602\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Garden-Centre-Social-Media.jpg 1122w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Garden-Centre-Social-Media-360x450.jpg 360w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Garden-Centre-Social-Media-750x937.jpg 750w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1122px) 100vw, 1122px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Organic and Paid: Two Halves of the Same Engine</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Social marketing runs on two engines, and the best programs use both.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Organic social is the content you publish without paying for reach: posts, reels, stories, and community engagement. Organic builds trust and personality over time. It shows customers who you are, answers their questions, and keeps you visible to people who already follow you. It is slow, compounding, and hard to fake, which is exactly why it matters.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Paid social is the amplification layer. With paid, you put budget behind a message so it reaches people beyond your existing followers, targeted by location, interests, behaviour, and more. Paid is how you reach new audiences quickly and scale what is working.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Treating these as an either/or choice is a common mistake. Organic without paid stays small. Paid without organic feels hollow, because prospects who click your ad and then find an empty, neglected profile rarely convert. The two work together: organic earns credibility, and paid extends your reach to the people who have never heard of you.</p>\n\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kb-btns12600_88e39c-02{gap:var(--global-kb-gap-xs, 0.5rem );justify-content:center;align-items:center;}.kt-btns12600_88e39c-02 .kt-button{font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;}.kt-btns12600_88e39c-02 .kt-btn-wrap-0{margin-right:5px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_88e39c-02 .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button{color:#555555;border-color:#555555;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_88e39c-02 .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button:hover, .wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_88e39c-02 .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button:focus{color:#ffffff;border-color:#444444;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_88e39c-02 .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button::before{display:none;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_88e39c-02 .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button:hover, .wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn.kt-btns12600_88e39c-02 .kt-btn-wrap-0 .kt-button:focus{background:#444444;}</style>\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn kb-buttons-wrap kb-btns12600_88e39c-02\"><style>ul.menu .wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn .kb-btn12600_ff4d13-84.kb-button{width:initial;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn .kb-btn12600_ff4d13-84.kb-button{color:var(--global-palette3, #1A202C);font-size:16px;font-family:Poppins;font-weight:400;text-transform:uppercase;border-top-left-radius:20px;border-top-right-radius:20px;border-bottom-right-radius:20px;border-bottom-left-radius:20px;border-top-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-top-style:solid;border-right-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-bottom-style:solid;border-left-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-left-style:solid;padding-right:var(--global-kb-spacing-md, 2rem);padding-left:var(--global-kb-spacing-md, 2rem);}@media all and (max-width: 1024px){.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn .kb-btn12600_ff4d13-84.kb-button{border-top-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-top-style:solid;border-right-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-bottom-style:solid;border-left-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-left-style:solid;}}@media all and (max-width: 767px){.wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn .kb-btn12600_ff4d13-84.kb-button{border-top-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-top-style:solid;border-right-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-bottom-style:solid;border-left-color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);border-left-style:solid;}}</style><a class=\"kb-button kt-button button kb-btn12600_ff4d13-84 kt-btn-size-standard kt-btn-width-type-auto kb-btn-global-outline kt-btn-has-text-true kt-btn-has-svg-false wp-block-kadence-singlebtn\" href=\"https://staging.kosick.com/services/social-media-marketing/\"><span class=\"kt-btn-inner-text\">Social Media marketing</span></a></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Where Social Marketing Fits in the Buying Journey</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Not every customer is ready to buy today, and social marketing is powerful because it meets people at every stage.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At the awareness stage, social introduces your brand to people who did not know you existed. A well-targeted video or a useful post plants the seed. At the consideration stage, social keeps you present while prospects compare options, through helpful content, testimonials, and proof you can deliver. At the decision stage, social closes the gap with retargeting, offers, and clear calls to action aimed at people who already showed interest.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A strong program is not obsessed with one stage. It builds a mix of content and campaigns so the top of the funnel stays full while the bottom keeps converting. When those pieces connect, social stops being a cost centre and starts behaving like a growth channel.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What a Good Social Marketing Program Includes</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you want the channel to produce, a few fundamentals need to be in place.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A clear audience definition comes first. You cannot write a message worth reading until you know exactly who is reading it and what they care about. Vague targeting produces vague results.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Next is a content plan built around themes and goals, not last-minute ideas. Consistency beats intensity. A steady rhythm of relevant content will always outperform a burst of posts followed by weeks of silence.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Platform fit matters too. What works on LinkedIn rarely works on Instagram, and TikTok is a different language again. Choosing the right platforms for your audience, and adapting the message to each, is half the battle.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Finally, measurement ties it all together. Reach, engagement, clicks, leads, and cost per result tell you what is working and what to cut. Without tracking, you are guessing, and guessing is expensive.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The businesses that struggle with social usually make the same handful of errors. They post inconsistently, appearing for a week and then vanishing. They talk only about themselves instead of solving a customer problem. They boost random posts with no strategy and call it advertising. And they judge success by vanity metrics like follower counts rather than by leads and sales.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">None of these are fatal on their own. Together, they are why so many owners conclude &#8220;social does not work for us.&#8221; It is not the channel. It is the approach.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Should You Manage Social In-House or Bring in Help?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Some businesses run social well in-house, especially when they have a dedicated person with the time and skill to plan, create, and analyze. Many do not, and social becomes one more thing squeezed in between everything else. The result is thin content and inconsistent effort.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is where an experienced partner earns its keep. A team living in these platforms every day knows what performs, how to stretch a budget, and how to connect social activity to real business outcomes. If social has felt like a chore or a guessing game, that outside perspective can be the difference between noise and growth.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Bottom Line</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Social marketing is not about being everywhere or chasing the latest trend. It is about using social platforms with intent: reaching the right people, guiding them toward a decision, and measuring what you get back. Done well, it builds brand, generates leads, and turns followers into customers.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you are ready to make social a channel that actually drives your business forward,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://kosick.com/services/social-media-marketing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\">Kosick Communications</a>&nbsp;builds and manages social marketing programs designed around your goals, not vanity metrics.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://kosick.com/contact/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\">Get in touch</a>&nbsp;and let us show you what a strategic approach can do.</p>\n\n\n<style>.kb-row-layout-id12600_cb9b0e-df > .kt-row-column-wrap{align-content:start;}:where(.kb-row-layout-id12600_cb9b0e-df > .kt-row-column-wrap) > .wp-block-kadence-column{justify-content:start;}.kb-row-layout-id12600_cb9b0e-df > .kt-row-column-wrap{column-gap:var(--global-kb-gap-md, 2rem);row-gap:var(--global-kb-gap-md, 2rem);max-width:700px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-top:50px;padding-bottom:50px;grid-template-columns:minmax(0, 1fr);}.kb-row-layout-id12600_cb9b0e-df > .kt-row-layout-overlay{opacity:0.30;}@media all and (max-width: 1024px){.kb-row-layout-id12600_cb9b0e-df > .kt-row-column-wrap{grid-template-columns:minmax(0, 1fr);}}@media all and (max-width: 767px){.kb-row-layout-id12600_cb9b0e-df > .kt-row-column-wrap{grid-template-columns:minmax(0, 1fr);}}</style><div class=\"kb-row-layout-wrap kb-row-layout-id12600_cb9b0e-df alignfull has-theme-palette4-background-color kt-row-has-bg wp-block-kadence-rowlayout\"><div class=\"kt-row-column-wrap kt-has-1-columns kt-row-layout-equal kt-tab-layout-inherit kt-mobile-layout-row kt-row-valign-top\">\n<style>.kadence-column12600_8c5cd9-6b > .kt-inside-inner-col{display:flex;}.kadence-column12600_8c5cd9-6b > .kt-inside-inner-col,.kadence-column12600_8c5cd9-6b > .kt-inside-inner-col:before{border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;}.kadence-column12600_8c5cd9-6b > .kt-inside-inner-col{